    "difficulty_level": "H2",
    "difficulty_reason": "The surjectivity argument needs an integral coupled double induction that constructs compatible invariant extensions, special-invariant decompositions and free coordinate patterns with prescribed blocks. The proof controls forced coordinates through recursive algorithms over an arbitrary commutative ring, without semisimple decomposition or division. That new construction remains beyond ordinary qualification work even after tensor/partition-algebra foundations; its supporting properties are part of this one target.",
    "source_scope_note": "Prove exactly Theorem4.10: for any commutative unital ring, n>=2 and r>=1, the symmetric-group maps onto the partition and half-partition tensor centralizers are surjective. Both maps form one authored outcome. Complete new integral extension/decomposition, forced/free-coordinate algorithms, prescribed-block construction and coupled double induction retained. No opposite centralizer direction or supporting property receives a separate count. Ordinary free-module tensor algebra, partition-algebra notation and the precisely stated Schur--Weyl/centralizer background are original named prerequisites. The two-sided inverse verification of explicitly supplied excision/reinsertion maps in Proposition4.6 and commutation in4.9 are source-designated routine reader checks retained verbatim and disclosed; the actual maps and all substantive integral linear-system construction proofs remain here. Full original native body, figures, tables, formulas, proof order and percent guards retained byte-exact. Two repeated author hyperlink target names in native2330/2350 are made unique by a finite wrapper-only occurrence namespace; printed labels/prose/mathematics are untouched. The source left-to-reader checks and original administrative/illustrative context remain visible without assistant proof reconstruction. No publisher/private class executed.",
